But since you mentioned it, might as well be complete. The code
comments say:

 If hero is a wizard, their current intelligence
 (bonuses + temporary + current)
 affects hunger reduction in casting a spell.
 1. int = 17-18 no reduction
 2. int = 16    1/4 hungr
 3. int = 15    1/2 hungr
 4. int = 1-14  normal reduction
 The reason for this is:
 a) Intelligence affects the amount of exertion
 in thinking.
 b) Wizards have spent their life at magic and
 understand quite well how to cast spells.



(Note that in the code hunger reduction is more like nutrition
reduction or hunger increase).

So, depending on the stats he rolled, he may or may not want to be
casting light at every stairwell.

